error[E0484]: a callback can't take `f32[]` here
  --> tests/programs/c/views/e0484.la:3:35
  |
3 | extern fun on_block(f: direct fun(f32[], data), user: data);
  |                                   ^^^^^
  |
  = help: take `View<f32>`, which reads C's memory in place; `to_array()` copies it to keep

error[E0484]: a callback can't take `Ref<f32[]>` here
  --> tests/programs/c/views/e0484.la:4:34
  |
4 | extern fun on_fill(f: direct fun(Ref<f32[]>, data), user: data);
  |                                  ^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: take `MutView<f32>`: it writes C's memory in place, during the call

error[E0484]: a callback can't take `View<u8>` here
  --> tests/programs/c/views/e0484.la:5:35
  |
5 | extern fun on_late(f: spawned fun(View<u8>, data), user: data);
  |                                   ^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: a `spawned` callback runs after C's call returns, when C's memory may be gone: take `u8[]`, a copy

error[E0484]: a callback can't take `i64[]` here
  --> tests/programs/c/views/e0484.la:6:35
  |
6 | extern fun on_now(f: realtime fun(i64[], data), user: data);
  |                                   ^^^^^
  |
  = help: take `View<i64>`, which reads C's memory in place; `to_array()` copies it to keep

